{
  "requirement": "Usage MUST record each provider request's outcome and available input/output\ntoken counts, including retries, with cached or reasoning-token counts when\nprovided. Missing measurements MUST be recorded as unavailable, not zero.\nRun totals MUST include request and tool-call counts by tool, elapsed time, and\navailable token usage, identifying incomplete totals without double counting\nprovider counters that overlap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the sources satisfy `requirements.authoring.usage_requests`. The implementation covers each obligation and is marked `{impl}`. Tests cover the main cases. I could not check how rig fills its `Usage` counters for Bedrock and Ollama (they are in an external crate). The code only copies them and never adds subset counters into the totals.\n\n**Per-request outcome and tokens**\n- `assess` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` calls `usage.begin_request()` before every provider attempt, retries included.\n- It then calls `end_request(index, elapsed, response.ok().map(|r| &r.usage))` after each attempt, whether it succeeded or failed.\n- `end_request` in `src/authoring/usage.rs` records the outcome as `completed` or `failed` and stores the per-request elapsed time.\n- `begin_request` starts each request as `unfinished`, and `finish(\"cancelled\")` marks an in-flight request `cancelled`.\n- `bedrock_sdk_config` disables AWS SDK retries (`RetryConfig::disabled()`), so each provider attempt appears as its own recorded request and none is hidden inside the SDK.\n- `TokenCounts::from_usage` copies input, output, cached-input, cache-creation and reasoning counts as `Option<u64>`. The cached, cache-creation and reasoning counts are recorded only when the provider supplies them.\n\n**Missing means unavailable, not zero**\n- A failed request gets `TokenCounts::default()`, where every counter is `None` and serializes as `null`.\n- `sum_counter` returns `None` when no request measured a counter, and a real `0` stays `0`. The mixed test asserts `cached_input == 0` alongside a null `reasoning`.\n\n**Run totals**\n- `request_count` and `requests[]` hold the request counts.\n- `tool_calls`, `tool_failures` and `tool_skipped` are maps keyed by tool name, with a total `tool_call_count`.\n- `tool` and `skipped_tool` update these counts. Unknown tool names collapse to `\"unknown\"`.\n- `record.elapsed_ms` is refreshed on `begin_request`, `end_request` and `finish`.\n- `TokenCounts::sum` totals the available tokens.\n- It sets `complete = false` when any request lacks input or output counts, or when an optional counter was measured on only some requests. This also covers in-flight, failed and cancelled requests.\n- The comment in `sum` says cache and reasoning counters are subsets and are never added into the input or output totals, so overlapping counters are not double counted.\n\n**Tests**\n- `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown`: input 200 despite cached 60, an in-flight request is incomplete, and a `None` usage is recorded as failed with a null input.\n- `partial_failure_retains_available_totals_and_optional_measurements`: failed requests, partial and mixed optional counters.\n- `cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals`: cancelled outcome, elapsed time, incomplete totals.\n- `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text`: per-tool counts, failures, skips and the `\"unknown\"` bucket.\n- `throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt` (`src/authoring/mod.rs`): 8 failed attempts plus 1 completed attempt are all recorded, each failed one with `tokens.complete == false`.\n- The CLI and batch tests in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` and `tests/authoring_batch.rs` check end-to-end results:\n  - Ollama gives 22 input and 14 output tokens across 2 requests, with `complete == true` and 6 tool calls.\n  - Bedrock gives 38 input and 10 output tokens.\n  - A denied read gives `request_count == 1`, a tool failure and a `failed` outcome.\n\n**Marking:** I found no stray request-accounting code without an `{impl}` reference. The callers that finalize the log (`finish` in `author_evidence_with_output`, `prepare_assessment` and `PendingAssessment`) are marked for `usage_storage`, which covers persistence. The accounting behaviour in the `{impl}` code is within what this requirement specifies.",
  "inputs": [
